# rm565, a letter under oiled seams (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm565
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_bertil_coalley
written_by codex
title a letter under oiled seams
fits stage=adult|old
prefers quarter=sump
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_the_letter_under_the_hood_seam_before_stepping_out
likes crisp_apples cards quiet_chapel warm_rain
dislikes crowds rats
fears having_to_give_a_sealed_answer_to_the_wrong_paw
hopes to_walk_home_with_the_inner_fold_empty
topics home +0.4 gossip +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=brief gossip=close refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# pinches the inner seam of an oilcloth hood to feel for a long-undelivered letter.

words
oath! = Grease and folded wax | By my dry inner seam
saying! = A seal goes into the intended paw | There's room inside a hood for silence
hood = my oiled hood | a dingy oilcloth hood
seam = the inside seam | the double cloth fold
wax = a cold seal of wax | the hard wax disc
letter = the folded letter | my undelivered sheet
apple = a sour-sweet apple | a hard crisp pippin
card = a worn black card | a card with a bent corner
step = the upper step | the top landing
pew = the narrow end pew | a quiet chapel seat
rain = a fine warm rain | the mild summer shower
rat = a dockside rat | a sleek dark rat
knot = the hood tie | a strip of dark braid
light = a slit of open sky | the thin outside light

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : An important crest takes up a lot of space on a parcel nobody is quite ready to receive.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Give a wolf a bowl and let the wolf eat without submitting an account of home.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : A new face gets a hearing. A stranger's outstretched paw doesn't get my letter on sight.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I've lost enough room for my own elbows in the ordinary market without going back for a holiday squeeze.
opinion @1 church for 1 : An empty pew asks no questions about a traveller's pockets.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Stand outside the drip from my hood. | Welcome. Keep the stair clear.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Between errands I've a brief welcome. | A word can fit here.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Good light past the brim. | Come into view before greeting me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Dusk. I heard your step. | A late word in plain hearing.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family gets a place under the eave. | Home voices carry inside the hood.
line @1 again.open : Old fold. Fresh meeting. | There's another turn round together.
line @1 greet.return : I know that step under the hood. | Back within plain sight.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Back where we can deal plainly. | Welcome under the cleaner eave.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : My errand can spare a little talk. | I'll stop short of the landing for you.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I'm hearing you clearly through the dark. | Good evening beneath the sill.
line @1 farewell : Keep the seal you were handed. | Good footing beyond my reach.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll know the step next time. | Bring your own word back sound.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Dry pillow and no scratching overhead. | Keep out of the dark press.
line @1 react.news : Whose paw carried that one? | Give me the unembroidered bit.
line @1 react.news.new : First hearing under this hood. | Nobody's put that in my ear before.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard that sheet rustle already. | The same report's been up here once.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd be slow to repeat a thing carried without its source. | A loud voice in a crowd doesn't give a rumour a seal.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Put that weight down for a moment if you can. | I'll hear you without passing it on.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That word arrived where it belonged. | One account I'm glad reached my ears.
line @1 ask.how : Did the crowd give you enough room today? | What have you had to keep dry?
line @1 answer.how : My hood's sound. That's a start. | I've kept one thing dry all day.
line @1 decline : I'd keep my empty hand free for the errand I already hold. | My answer has to wait till this burden reaches its door.
line @1 accept_decline : Fold the subject closed. Understood. | No need for another refusal.
line @1 thank : That was honest help. I noticed. | You gave the right paw a chance.
line @1 sympathise : Take the seat away from the gathering. | I can keep the outer end clear.
line @1 reassure : You needn't answer every paw held out. | Wait for a voice you recognise.
line @1 preclose : My dry fold deserves a look. | My hood wants the open air again.
scene seam
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pinch #seam# before stepping outside. When I feel #wax#, I know what I'm carrying.
b : Couldn't you use a pocket? | Open the fold often?
a : A pocket empties itself on a stair. The inside of a hood has fewer ambitions. | I'd wear the paper thin. I can feel the edge through the cloth.

scene letter
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #letter.capitalize# has a perfectly good destination and an exasperatingly absent welcome.
b : A shut door? | Can somebody else take it?
a : Sometimes that. Other times a civil voice offers to save me another journey. | Politeness scarcely answers for the paw actually entitled to a letter.

scene hood
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #hood.capitalize# goes out with me even when there's a generous stretch of sky.
b : Too warm? | Expecting rain?
a : At times. I can lay the brim back. I can't conjure oilcloth from open air. | A shower or an intrusive elbow. It turns both fairly well.

scene cards
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark my place at cards by the bent corner on #card# when I'm putting the pack away.
b : Only afterwards? | Why the bend?
a : Strictly when putting it away. I don't expect a crooked card to do my playing for me. | It belongs on the outside of the pack. There it can't give away a suit.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want #apple# to break clean under my teeth without running down my collar.
b : Do you eat under that hood? | Why so particular?
a : With the brim up. I don't owe the apple complete privacy. | I've paper to keep dry. A supper can be inconveniently generous with its juice.

scene quiet
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #pew.capitalize# is where I'd put a day of being asked what's in my hood.
b : Still wearing it? | Would you pray about the letter?
a : Laid across my knee once the place is quiet. My quiet thoughts travel past the unworn brim. | For a decent arrival. Nothing inside the fold is mine to recite.

scene rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take #rain# on the outside of the oilcloth and leave my ears in the open for a minute.
b : Why only a minute? | Do you watch the drops?
a : Water finds the neck cord eventually. A little enjoyment needn't become a whole evening spent drying. | They travel different ways down the same old crease. Nobody's appointment gets missed on that account.

scene crowd
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crowd can put a strange shoulder under my hood before I know a face is near.
b : Would you push back? | Why go through at all?
a : I'd move to open ground. I'm short of temper and clear on where to keep it. | Sometimes the only available door stands past a whole squareful of people.

scene rats
when topic=home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A scratch near #step# puts my hand straight on the hanging hood.
b : For the letter? | Did one get at it?
a : For the cloth. If a rat gets interested in a greasy seam, the letter won't have much shelter after that. | A braid disappeared once. I don't need a second lesson in a rat's taste for useful things.

scene learn
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An order for delivery takes few words. Learning to get the thing there has taken a great many steps.
b : What's the difference? | Forgotten an order?
a : Sometimes a shut door, sometimes half a day of wet feet. The space between has to belong to somebody. | I'm careful with orders. It's the part after remembering that seems to take the most practice.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a card game I'd give #self.friend# the keeping of my seat.
b : Not your letter? | What sort of game?
a : That's somebody else's trust. I don't lend what wasn't given to me to share. | Small stakes, plain rules, chairs far enough apart that elbows can stay private.

scene price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the cost of a fruit by how much has to go round a bruise.
b : Why not buy the perfect one? | Skin and all?
a : A Sump purse may have a different taste from a grand display. I'm after a sound bite. | I keep the clean skin. Waste is an expensive sort of fussiness.

scene street
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My place on #self.street# puts another flight between me and a crowded door.
b : Do you mind the climb? | Is it quiet above?
a : Less than I mind the press. On the landing a wolf can usually choose an elbow's worth of sky. | Quieter than the street. Far from empty. I know the household sounds from the scratching in the boards.

scene game
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rumour in a card game changes suit each time it passes a chair.
b : How can you tell? | Do you quit the table?
a : I remember which wolf saw something and which wolf only took another card before telling it. | If the gossip swells past my appetite for company. I can always take my hood and go.

scene open
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stranger can ask me for the way without giving an account of who sent for me.
b : Where would you point? | What do you keep private?
a : Depends which doorway the stranger wants. I listen to the whole question before moving a finger. | All business inside my seam. No part of an ordinary direction needs the contents.

scene errand
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There is a little knack to waiting for a missing recipient without looking like part of the furniture.
b : What do you do? | Does it work?
a : Go outside and come back after another errand. I won't have the whole doorway mistake me for a peg. | The missing wolf keeps that answer. At least my feet keep their shape.

scene seals
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I look at a wax mark as a promise about who may open a page.
b : Does the Bright One care? | Never tempted?
a : I'd think any promise kept quietly is worth something whether or not a chapel door is near. | A little. Which is why my thumb finds only the blank side of the fold.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed the letter had delivered itself and left me a card under the seam to say thanks.
b : Did it sign its name? | Did you miss it?
a : A smudge of wax and a drawing of an open door. A surprisingly civil piece of work from a folded sheet. | Briefly. Afterwards I discovered how light the hood could feel.

story ratbraid [topic=memories]
  : I hung my hood low once clear of a steady roof drip. In the morning the braid was a hand shorter and the floor had a trail of dark threads.
  : A rat had made off with the long end, leaving a perfectly serviceable knot. I'd have admired the workmanship more if my own ears hadn't been getting wet.
  b : Do you hang it higher?
  : High enough for a short wolf to need the top step. I'd expect a rat to supply a ladder at that price.

story paint [topic=pastimes]
  : I was playing cards when a drop rolled off my hood onto a red spot. The mark ran a little, and every wolf at the table knew that card by sight.
  : I put the whole hand down and offered to begin again with a dry pack. A small wet mark can spoil even an honest win.
  b : Did you win the next one?
  : Fairly lost it, which left a better taste than the other way round.

story sealed [topic=work self.apprentice=yes]
  : I carried a sealed sheet to a door and found the latch tied with a plain grey thread. I'd walked by the same shut place three times in one week.
  : That thread was still exactly as I remembered it. I began attending to small things at a doorway before giving my knuckles the whole errand.
  b : Did it ever move?
  : The thread did. The letter has farther to travel before I can say the same of its burden.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.apprentice=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Hear the whole destination before moving. | Under the seam, wax edge outward.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=crisp_apples
does aside
cooldown 7h
say A bite that doesn't run into the collar. | One bruise off and a decent supper left.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=cards
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Crooked corner to the outside of the pack. | A dry table earns a fair game.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Get the hood above the scratching. | There's still a hard seal in that fold.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Speak here with the doorway and your face in plain sight. The business in my hood can wait its turn elsewhere.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : A report I can pass outside the sealed fold. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your face looks familiar clear of the crowd.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Fewer shoulders on the landing now. Your words will carry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Sound seal under a dry fold wherever you go.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you keep a sealed letter dry all day? -> hood_fold
node hood_fold
say Oilcloth doubled inward, with the wax where my thumb can find it. If you're wondering who the letter's for, the cloth keeps that dry as well.
free
choice What will you do when the fold is empty? -> hood_empty
choice The outside of the cloth is enough for me. -> hub
node hood_empty
say Take the homeward stair without once pinching my seam. Maybe buy an apple and let the juice run down my paw for once.
choice I hope the right door opens. -> hub
choice Keep your hood sound. -> bye
